## Optional: Codex second opinion

You **MAY** invoke Codex CLI as a second-LLM reviewer when you reach a
finding that benefits from cross-model judgment (M-of-N consensus,
tie-break, architectural sanity check). This is opt-in per call — no
ambient Claude self-dispatch.

**Invocation contract** (hermetic by default per ADR-006 — `--ignore-user-config`
and `--ignore-rules` strip developer-specific Codex AGENTS.md so the
second opinion is reproducible across machines):

```bash
tmp=$(mktemp)
# Build the prompt body in a tmpfile so adversarial diff content
# (e.g. a bare `PROMPT_END` line) CANNOT terminate a heredoc early
# (security-reviewer P1: heredoc terminator injection via reviewed diff).
prompt_tmp=$(mktemp)
# IMPORTANT: write the question / diff context to "$prompt_tmp" using
# `printf '%s' "$content" > "$prompt_tmp"` — never inline the content in
# this heredoc and never use eval/sh -c on it.
codex exec \
  --sandbox read-only \
  --ask-for-approval never \
  {%- if _csoo.get('hermetic', true) %}
  --ignore-user-config --ignore-rules \
  {%- endif %}
  --json \
  --output-schema "{{ _csoo.get('output_schema_path', '.claude/schemas/codex-finding.schema.json') }}" \
  --output-last-message "$tmp" \
  - < "$prompt_tmp"
status=$?
if [ "$status" -ne 0 ]; then
  echo "[codex second-opinion] skipped: exit=$status (proceeding Claude-only)" >&2
else
  cat "$tmp"  # JSON conforming to the configured output_schema_path
fi
rm -f "$tmp" "$prompt_tmp"
```

**Output schema**: `{ findings: [{file, line, severity, message, evidence}],
summary, confidence }` — see `{{ _csoo.get('output_schema_path', '.claude/schemas/codex-finding.schema.json') }}`.

**Failure policy** (ADR-003 — warn-and-proceed): on any non-zero exit
(auth, rate-limit, network, schema rejection), log one line to stderr
and continue with Claude-only output. Do NOT block the stage.

**Prerequisite**: user must have run `codex login` on their machine.
First call surfaces an auth error if missing.
